    "long_instructions": "Welcome to your first web page project! You're going to build a web page all about your pet fish.\r\n\r\nOpen up the `index.html` file. You'll see some basic HTML tags already there: `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>`. These tags are like the main sections of a book, telling the browser how to structure your page.\r\n\r\nYour first task is to give your web page a title. Find the `<head>` section in `index.html`. Inside the `<head>` tags, add a new tag called `<title>`. Between the opening `<title>` and closing `</title>` tags, type `My Pet Fish Page`.\r\n\r\nWhen you're done, your page will have a proper title that shows up in the browser tab!",
    "generate_outline": "Students will create a basic HTML file with `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags. They will add a `<title>` tag inside the `<head>` to set the web page's title to 'My Pet Fish Page'."
